  "title": "Explain an exercise through the conversation",
  "message": "Differentiate your content by contrasting common advice with what you actually believe.",
  "arc": "Audience promise \u2192 shared-information problem \u2192 two-column exercise \u2192 contrarian position \u2192 useful differentiation.",
  "foundation": "The viewer needs the argument and the speaker's explanation, rather than a second permanent surface. This is a useful contrast to CR07 from the same podcast setting: an exercise can remain conversational when its structure is simple enough to follow.",
  "execution": "Preserve eyes, hands and listener reactions. Keep ordinary captions near the face without covering expression. Clear the temporary red promise once the explanation is established. A simple two-column aid is a possible adaptation if the new speech makes the contrast hard to retain; it is not an observed graphic in this reel.",
  "avoid": "Do not infer that mentioning paper requires stock paper footage. Do not put an empty diagram next to every interview. The exercise itself is not demonstrated on a legible sheet here.",
  "typography": "Small white sentence-case speech captions; a larger white opening promise on red backing. Exact font identity is unverified; transfer hierarchy and lifetime, not the red brand treatment.",
